He's pretty dirty.

46
00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:34.000
Hmm.

47
00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.200
Lucky for you. mister.
you're just a starvin' animal.

48
00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.400
Yeah.

49
00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.500
- Ah. Señor...
- Take it easy. Max.

50
00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:58.400
You gotta last another 12 hours.

51
00:07:58.500 --> 00:07:59.800
You ain't worth a cent dead.

52
00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.900
He'll make it 'til tomorrow.

53
00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.388
Hey. can you imagine
what he's gonna look like...

54
00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:10.300
when they hang him tomorrow?

55
00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.100
He'll be dangling like puppet.

56
00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.300
Yeah.

57
00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:16.200
Hey. you take it easy there. Chico.

58
00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.800
You get all excited.
you're gonna bust a gut.

59
00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:31.800
Feel almost human now. don't ya?

60
00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.000
Yeah.

61
00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.100
You just take it easy there now. max.

62
00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.300
Si. señor.

63
00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:51.000
- Vamos. hombre. let's go.
- What'd you say?

64
00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.100
Come on. get up.

65
00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.900
You know. Sage. least you could do...

66
00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.300
for a man who wants
to die is to wish him...

67
00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.100
a cross with his name on it.

68
00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.500
You just give him your name.
you'll get one.

69
00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:08.100
They call me Trinity.

70
00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:10.800
- Trinity?
- Mm-hmm.

71
00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.400
- Well. that's...
- Right-hand of the devil.

72
00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:20.200
Come on. move.

73
00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:24.100
How much do I owe ya?

74
00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.900
Uh. nada- nothing. on the house.

75
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.600
Thanks.

76
00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.700
The beans weren't much good. anyway.

77
00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:35.888
Señor. they're going to shoot you.

78
00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:38.500
- Shh.
- Hey. Trinity.

79
00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.600
They say you got the fastest gun around.

80
00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:47.100
- Is that what they say?
- Yeah.

81
00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.500
- Geez.

82
00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:04.800
Okay. Chico.
suppose you tell us what happened. huh?

83
00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.200
There was a gringo. Señor.

84
00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.500
He want to make love to my mujer...

85
00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.700
so I push him away with a little knife.

86
00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.000
A very little knife. señor.

87
00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.300
Oh. but when I look into his black eyes...

88
00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:20.800
they turn white.
and he falls down to the ground.

89
00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:22.300
Bada-boom.

90
00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:24.000
He must have hit his head.

91
00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.000
Must've at that.

92
00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.400
Yeah. I think so. too. señor.

93
00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:28.300
Any witnesses?

94
00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:31.300
- No. only me.
- Think hard now. Chico.

95
00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.000
You mean my wife and the knife. señor?

96
00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:35.000
- And me.
- Hah!

97
00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.100
Oh. no. there was only this gringo...

98
00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.800
and he want to make love to my wife.

99
00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.600
Yeah. I know. and you pushed him away...

100
00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.500
with a very little knife.

101
00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.000
Si. Señor.

102
00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.500
Hah!

103
00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.400
Clear out and leave me in peace!

104
00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.500
We'll go when we're ready.

105
00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.300
You're the one that's
lookin' for trouble now!

106
00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.600
Look. can't you see I'm busy?

107
00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:53.500
So are we!

108
00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.000
Only one way to let him know now.

109
00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:00.000
Yeah. the hard way.

110
00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:07.300
Go on. go.
Be good boy.

111
00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.300
- Sheriff!
- Go away.

112
00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:13.300
Scat!

113
00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:16.500
If you want that tin star
to see the sun again...

114
00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:19.000
you better set our friend free.

115
00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:21.500
He crawled into a woman's bed.

116
00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:24.100
She wanted him out. he didn't get out.

117
00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:26.300
They call that carnal violence.

118
00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.900
He's gonna have to go before the judge.

119
00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.000
How do you expect the judge
to see it straight?

120
00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.900
That old bag was his wife.
and she woulda stayed there...

121
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.200
too. if the old man hadn't a come in.

122
00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:38.200
She was purrin' sweet up until then.

123
00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.100
Your friend chose the wrong bed.

124
00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:42.500
The law is the law.
and strange as it may seem...

125
00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:46.000
to the likes of you.
the law is gonna be respected.

126
00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:50.200
Now.
you got exactly one minute to split town.

127
00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:52.600
This is the last warning. sheriff.

128
00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:55.000
Let our friend out!

129
00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.200
Boys. I have the impression...

130
00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.800
we're going to have to elect a new sheriff.

131
00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:32.400
- You wanna run. Jeff?
- Not a chance.

132
00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:08.100
Hey. you!
Stinkweed!

133
00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.200
You mean me?

134
00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.600
Yeah. I mean you. rag picker!

135
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.700
I think he means you.

136
00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.800
Drop that holster!

137
00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:32.100
Huh.

138
00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:38.500
Now it's your turn. Sheriff- drop it!

139
00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:51.400
They'll be stiff before they can draw.

140
00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.200
- What did I tell you?
- Madre Mia.

141
00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:03.000
Who is he. Señor?

142
00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:06.900
The left hand of the devil.

143
00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:19.000
Never woulda believed it.

144
00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:27.400
- Who's that?
- Oh. it's a long story.

145
00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.200
He's up for ransom.
You know how it is.

146
00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.800
The Mexicans are always wrong.

147
00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:32.600
- What's he have to say?
- Nothin'...

148
00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.300
Self defense with witnesses to the fact.

149
00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.200
Write him a pardon and send him home.

150
00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:37.620
No. Señor Sheriff. it's not true.

151
00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:41.000
There were no peoples.
It was only this gringo.

152
00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.500
He want to...
he want to make love...

153
00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:45.900
Oh. stop it.

154
00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.900
He want to make love to my mujer. señor.

155
00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.900
Here.

156
00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.200
It's a bad wound.

157
00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.100
Lucky for him.
the bullet plugged up the vein.

158
00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.900
Give me a hand.

159
00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:21.700
- Anesthesia?
- Si. Señor.

160
00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.300
Yeah.

161
00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.100
Oh. that's a very big knife.

162
00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:36.000
No. very little.
Here. have some more.

163
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.300
Here.

164
00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:58.300
- Another swig. hmm?
- Mm-hmm.

165
00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.300
- How's the old lady?
- The same.

166
00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.400
She's always got something wrong with her.

167
00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:10.200
Now. where the devil is it?

168
00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.600
In New Orleans. runnin' a whore house.

169
00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:14.100
I was talkin' about the bullet.

170
00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:18.500
There it is.

171
00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.400
Hmm.

172
00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:31.100
Put your finger in it.

173
00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:57.400
You gringos are over here with your burros.

174
00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:59.188
- That's right.
- You make love to our señoras...

175
00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:00.500
and want to sleep.

176
00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:03.200
Good idea-go on to sleep.

177
00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.600
Sweet dreams.

178
00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:17.500
Tomorrow. you can take him back
to his beloved mujer.

179
00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.300
You're still quick on the draw. I see.

180
00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:28.500
That reminds me.
Thanks for your help.

181
00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:31.500
There were only three.

182
00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:34.400
Yeah. for now. but let me tell ya.

183
00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:37.400
They'll be swarmin' into this damn town.

184
00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.200
You'd do better to get outta here before...

185
00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:43.700
all the dudes in the west
fall in to match guns.

186
00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:46.700
Well. I'm not lookin' for trouble.

187
00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:50.000
Yeah.
you never knew how to do anything else.

188
00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:03.000
Smells like a distillery in here.

189
00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:10.200
- Who is he?
- My brother.

190
00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:13.300
He's just passin' through.

191
00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.600
He's leavin' tomorrow.

192
00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:19.800
He looked and smelled like that.
too. when he came here.

193
00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:23.600
Had to use three pieces of soap
to see the color of his skin.

194
00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:26.700
So. young man. if you wanna shake my hand.
take a bath first.

195
00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:28.800
Don't wanna catch no tetanus.

196
00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.800
Ah. now what's that?

197
00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.800
How'd you end up like this?

198
00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:39.500
Ah. there was somebody following me.

199
00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.800
The owner of the star.

200
00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:44.800
Mm-hmm.

201
00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:47.100
- Downright disgusting.
- Hey. gringo...

202
00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:50.200
Two days after...
two days after my escape...

203
00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:53.100
from the penitentiary in Yuma...

204
00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:56.300
I saw somebody following me.

205
00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:58.000
He wasn't after me.

206
00:19:58.100 --> 00:19:59.800
We were just going the same way...

207
00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:02.600
but I didn't know that. and I shot him.

208
00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:05.400
Found out later
he was the new sheriff of this town...

209
00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:07.900
come to replace the one that was killed.

210
00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:11.300
There was this here star
in one of his pockets...

211
00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:14.100
so I took his place to wait for my men...

212
00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:16.400
and head for California together.

213
00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:18.200
I planned a couple of good hold-ups...

214
00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:20.800
but I bet you'll manage
to mess things up on me.

215
00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.300
I don't know how.
but I'm sure you'll do it.

216
00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:24.900
Hmm.

217
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.800
This isn't a jail. it's a cesspool!

218
00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.800
Which reminds me...
while you were out of town...

219
00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:31.700
there was a real slaughter at the saloon.

220
00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:34.700
The Major's men just pounded
two of those farmers.

221
00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:37.800
And from now on.
they'll eat nothin' but puddin'...

222
00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:41.500
'cause they left their teeth
on the bar room floor.

223
00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:44.400
Hmm.
Were they armed?

224
00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:46.700
Those farmers don't go around armed.

225
00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:49.600
You know that. Sheriff.
Come on. young fella.

226
00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:52.000
Let's get home and give yourself a bath...

227
00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:53.900
and see what you look like.

228
00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.900
- Well...
- You get washed up...

229
00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.500
and tomorrow you leave.
- See ya later.

230
00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:02.200
No. you're not gonna see me later!

231
00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:05.200
You sure you two fellas are brothers?

232
00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:06.700
Yep.

233
00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.600
- Same mother.
- Oh.

234
00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:37.000
I ain't seen so much dirt
since the overflow of the Pecos.

235
00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:43.300
It's the last piece!

236
00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:45.900
From what I understand.
there's a lotta dirt in this town. too.

237
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:48.100
Well.
if you're referring to the Major's men...

238
00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:50.100
he just won't let up on those farmers.

239
00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:54.000
He keeps breakin' their bones.
and they come back for more.

240
00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:56.300
Hard as nails. them farmers.

241
00:21:56.700 --> 00:22:00.600
- Well. why don't they fight back?
- Against their principles.

242
00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:04.600
Strange folks from back East.

243
00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:08.600
All they do. is. uh.
work and pray. pray and work.

244
00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:10.800
Pray and work is all they do.

245
00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:16.300
What's my brother doin' about it?

246
00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:18.700
Beans... that's what he's doin' about it.

247
00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:19.800
You know somethin'?

248
00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:23.000
I've never seen such an unlucky sheriff
in all my life.

249
00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:25.700
When somethin' happens.
he's someplace else...

250
00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:27.100
and vice versa.

251
00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:30.400
- He's always been very unlucky.
- Yeah.

252
00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:35.088
If I'd known you were gonna
put on them rags...

253
00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:38.700
I wouldn't have given you
that last piece of soap.

254
00:22:40.600 --> 00:22:42.900
- Evening. Sheriff.
- Shut up.

255
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:46.900
- What's got into him?
- The usual nightly scolding.

256
00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:50.400
- The Major's men?
- Yep.

257
00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:52.000
Well. g'bye. young fella.

258
00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:54.500
I'm gonna take my bones to bed.

259
00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:57.900
In case I don't see you again.
uh. which is likely...

260
00:22:58.000 --> 00:22:59.800
good luck to ya. huh?

261
00:23:03.700 --> 00:23:06.900
Listen. Major.
I'm gettin' a little weary...

262
00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.900
of these punks of yours.

263
00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:10.900
Either they let the farmers be...

264
00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:14.400
or I'll have to take away their guns.

265
00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:16.800
Why don't you do it?

266
00:23:16.900 --> 00:23:19.600
Yeah. how about that. Sheriff?

267
00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:21.600
Hmm.

268
00:23:33.700 --> 00:23:36.100
They're good boys. Sheriff.

269
00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:38.600
Hard workin' cowhands
need a little diversion...

270
00:23:38.700 --> 00:23:40.700
when Saturday night rolls around.

271
00:23:40.800 --> 00:23:43.100
Like squattin' helpless farmers. huh?

272
00:23:43.200 --> 00:23:45.200
Well. what do you expect?

273
00:23:45.300 --> 00:23:47.900
If the farmers insist
on provoking trouble...

274
00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:50.000
a few fists are gonna start flyin'.

275
00:23:50.100 --> 00:23:54.000
It's only human nature.
Or. would you know about that?

276
00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:57.200
Now. I heartily suggest that you go
about your business...

277
00:23:57.300 --> 00:23:59.600
and leave me and my men in peace.

278
00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:04.800
Put it any way you want. Major...
this is the last warning...

279
00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:07.600
for you and for your chicken rustlers.

280
00:24:08.500 --> 00:24:10.800
What did you say?

281
00:24:11.900 --> 00:24:13.900
Chicken rustlers.

282
00:24:14.300 --> 00:24:16.200
Oh.

283
00:24:17.700 --> 00:24:21.700
You have the strangest way
of doin' your job. Sheriff.

284
00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:25.000
And let me tell you...

285
00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:27.100
I don't like it.

286
00:24:35.700 --> 00:24:38.000
Listen. boys.

287
00:24:39.200 --> 00:24:41.400
Come on. slug. pull out.

288
00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:44.600
What the devil is the matter with you.
Jeff?

289
00:24:53.600 --> 00:24:56.900
This sheriff's beginning to bother me.

290
00:24:57.300 --> 00:25:01.800
He's a bit too dull to appreciate
my position in this town.

291
00:25:02.200 --> 00:25:04.500
Well. he'll learn the hard way.

292
00:25:04.600 --> 00:25:08.400
They work like ants.
but that don't soften the Major none...

293
00:25:08.700 --> 00:25:12.200
he wants to hog up their whole valley
for his horses.

294
00:25:12.300 --> 00:25:14.500
What do you care?
You're not the sheriff.

295
00:25:14.600 --> 00:25:16.900
Yeah. yeah. I know.

296
00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:20.600
But if he stirs up enough fuss.
the rangers will get here...

297
00:25:20.800 --> 00:25:24.200
before my boys.
Weasel and Timmy. can catch up with me.

298
00:25:24.300 --> 00:25:28.200
Besides. on principle.
I hate to see him win out.

299
00:25:28.300 --> 00:25:29.600
Why?

300
00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:32.600
Because two feet this side of the valley...

301
00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:34.500
he's got the most
beautiful pack of horses...

302
00:25:34.600 --> 00:25:37.800
I ever seen.
Unbranded.

303
00:25:37.900 --> 00:25:41.300
Once he drives the farmers out
and brings his herd in...

304
00:25:41.400 --> 00:25:44.600
what chance have I got
to rustle 'em back out again?

305
00:25:44.700 --> 00:25:47.400
- So. give 'em a hand.
- Who. the Major?

306
00:25:47.500 --> 00:25:49.900
The farmers.

307
00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:52.800
Ah. it's easier said than done.

308
00:25:52.900 --> 00:25:56.500
Can't even root up
a-a hoot owl in this here town...

309
00:25:56.600 --> 00:25:59.400
that's willing to face the Major's men.

310
00:25:59.500 --> 00:26:01.700
And I can't do it all alone.

311
00:26:08.600 --> 00:26:10.400
Oh. no.

312
00:26:11.100 --> 00:26:12.700
Oh. yes.

313
00:26:13.400 --> 00:26:15.100
No.

314
00:26:15.600 --> 00:26:18.300
- A dollar a day.
- No.

315
00:26:18.700 --> 00:26:21.000
And ammunition.

316
00:26:22.400 --> 00:26:24.500
With room and board.

317
00:26:25.700 --> 00:26:29.100
And you get ol' Jonathan
to cook and wait on ya.

318
00:26:33.500 --> 00:26:34.900
Okay?

319
00:26:36.900 --> 00:26:38.000
No.

320
00:26:39.500 --> 00:26:42.900
Then get your carcass
outta here and leave me be!

321
00:26:58.000 --> 00:27:00.300
Hah. hah. hah!

322
00:27:09.700 --> 00:27:12.100
Looks like they're plannin' to settle down.

323
00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:15.100
That ain't no moonlight
camp they're buildin'. Major.

324
00:27:15.200 --> 00:27:18.000
Not if we persuade them differently.

325
00:27:18.100 --> 00:27:21.700
Boys. show the brethren
how to build a decent house.

326
00:27:21.800 --> 00:27:25.700
That structure doesn't strike me
as being very sturdy.

327
00:27:25.800 --> 00:27:27.800
This is time for work.
We can play later.

328
00:27:27.900 --> 00:27:29.600
Go on.

329
00:27:59.400 --> 00:28:01.900
- Welcome. Major.
- Are you sure?

330
00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:03.700
We're not given to lying. Major.

331
00:28:03.800 --> 00:28:06.400
Only to shadin' the truth.

332
00:28:06.500 --> 00:28:08.400
If. by some dark miracle...

333
00:28:08.500 --> 00:28:11.000
I should vanish before your eyes...

334
00:28:11.100 --> 00:28:14.200
I sincerely doubt you'd feel any remorse.

335
00:28:14.300 --> 00:28:17.000
We crave no such miracle.
but only for...

336
00:28:17.100 --> 00:28:19.800
a sense of dignity in our poverty.

337
00:28:19.900 --> 00:28:23.200
Oh. there is nothin' more aggravatin'
than a hypocrite.

338
00:28:24.300 --> 00:28:26.200
Now. you came here in a wagon...

339
00:28:26.300 --> 00:28:28.100
with a few rags and a lotta hope.

340
00:28:28.200 --> 00:28:29.800
A lot of faith. Major.

341
00:28:29.900 --> 00:28:31.900
Yes. and. by sheer coincidence...

342
00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:33.100
after a few months...

343
00:28:33.200 --> 00:28:37.100
more of your so-called brothers arrived.

344
00:28:37.200 --> 00:28:40.400
And good ol' faith forms a community...

345
00:28:40.500 --> 00:28:42.300
builds a house that
could shelter an army...

346
00:28:42.400 --> 00:28:46.100
and. uh. fills the corrals with livestock.

347
00:28:46.200 --> 00:28:49.200
Now. yours is certainly a very dignified...

348
00:28:49.300 --> 00:28:52.200
and. uh. lucrative poverty.

349
00:28:52.400 --> 00:28:54.600
It was wild cattle by God sent.

350
00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:58.900
Which. however. you branded quickly enough.

351
00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:01.000
And while my horses split their hooves...

352
00:29:01.100 --> 00:29:04.700
grazing on rocks. your cows grow fat...

353
00:29:04.800 --> 00:29:07.700
and shamelessly prolific like you.

354
00:29:07.900 --> 00:29:11.100
We sought but a small square of land
on which to live.

355
00:29:11.300 --> 00:29:12.700
But this small square...

356
00:29:12.800 --> 00:29:15.700
covers over 200.000 acres.
my friend.

357
00:29:15.800 --> 00:29:19.000
We ask only a small part of it.
There's land for all.

358
00:29:19.500 --> 00:29:21.400
Bring your horses to graze here.

359
00:29:21.500 --> 00:29:23.800
We will not resent their presence.

360
00:29:23.900 --> 00:29:26.500
No. but they'd resent yours.

361
00:29:26.900 --> 00:29:29.700
Now. I advise you to pack up your goods...

362
00:29:29.800 --> 00:29:32.500
your people. your faith. and your cows...

363
00:29:32.600 --> 00:29:34.500
and clear out of my valley.

364
00:29:34.700 --> 00:29:37.900
- We've come 2.000 miles.
- You can go another 2.000.

365
00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:41.300
- We have children. Major.
- Oh. I hate children.

366
00:29:41.500 --> 00:29:44.800
Major.
I've tried to appeal to your sentiments...

367
00:29:44.900 --> 00:29:47.200
but you force me now to remind you...

368
00:29:47.300 --> 00:29:50.700
that we came to this valley before you.

369
00:29:53.300 --> 00:29:56.300
I believe it was the Lord
in one of his parables...

370
00:29:56.400 --> 00:29:59.200
who said. "blessed are the last..."

371
00:29:59.300 --> 00:30:02.200
"for they shall be the first."

372
00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:05.100
So. why should I hurry?

373
00:30:05.200 --> 00:30:09.100
- It is evil to be cynical.
- It's practical.

374
00:30:09.200 --> 00:30:11.200
- May the lord forgive you.
- Well. I hope so...

375
00:30:11.300 --> 00:30:13.100
but I wouldn't count on it very much.

376
00:30:13.200 --> 00:30:14.100
- Hah!
- Hey!

377
00:30:14.200 --> 00:30:15.100
- Yam. yam.
- Rah. ha'. hah'!

378
00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:16.900
Hah. hah!

379
00:30:20.900 --> 00:30:23.700
Let this be a reminder. old man.

380
00:30:23.800 --> 00:30:27.700
Either you leave this valley.
or I'll bury you in it.

381
00:30:28.700 --> 00:30:31.200
The choice is yours.

382
00:30:32.300 --> 00:30:34.200
Let's go. boys!

383
00:30:40.100 --> 00:30:42.400
- Hah!
- Hah. hah. hah!

384
00:30:45.500 --> 00:30:48.600
- Yah. yah. yah!
- Hah. yah!

385
00:30:50.600 --> 00:30:52.800
To work. brothers. to work!

386
00:30:55.700 --> 00:30:57.000
Hold it!

387
00:31:03.600 --> 00:31:06.500
- Who are they?
- It's Mezcal and his raiders. Major.

388
00:31:06.600 --> 00:31:08.700
Once in a while.
they rustle a few horses from us.

389
00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:11.500
Well. that's very interesting.

390
00:31:29.300 --> 00:31:32.000
- Welcome. brothers.
- Thank you. brother.

391
00:31:38.900 --> 00:31:41.400
You forget that you are guests.

392
00:31:41.500 --> 00:31:44.200
Why don't you answer
brother Tobias' greeting?

393
00:31:47.500 --> 00:31:48.800
He's my brother.

394
00:31:48.900 --> 00:31:51.700
Now. you give this poor brother
something to eat. eh?

395
00:32:12.400 --> 00:32:15.700
- It doesn't taste like anything.
- We have no other food to offer.

396
00:32:15.800 --> 00:32:17.788
- You did it on purpose. Yes?
- No. it's not true. brother.

397
00:32:17.800 --> 00:32:19.720
You make this mess
so you don't have to share it.

398
00:32:19.800 --> 00:32:22.300
- No. we'd share anything we can.
- Lies. liar! Quiet!

399
00:32:24.800 --> 00:32:26.300
Shut up!

400
00:32:28.400 --> 00:32:30.500
Next time. no fooling around.

401
00:32:30.600 --> 00:32:33.200
I want good soup
with garlic and mucho vino!

402
00:32:34.400 --> 00:32:35.800
Vamonos.

403
00:32:46.400 --> 00:32:50.300
You know what that old fool
would say if he was in my place?

404
00:32:52.200 --> 00:32:55.300
The ways of the Lord are many.

405
00:33:38.300 --> 00:33:40.600
This is for the sheriff.

406
00:33:42.100 --> 00:33:45.500
- By the way. where is he?
- He went outta town.

407
00:34:02.800 --> 00:34:05.700
I thought your brother said
you were leavin' town today!

408
00:34:05.800 --> 00:34:08.200
The day ain't over yet!

409
00:34:13.100 --> 00:34:14.488
Hey. you wanna bet somethin'
is gonna happen...

410
00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:16.300
now that he's out of town?

411
00:34:20.300 --> 00:34:23.700
Hey. I'm talkin' to ya!
You wanna bet?

412
00:34:33.400 --> 00:34:35.288
Brother Tobias said.
if there's anything left over...

413
00:34:35.300 --> 00:34:38.300
we can get that nice bread.
Oh. I wonder if they still...

414
00:34:38.400 --> 00:34:39.800
have any of that bread.

415
00:34:40.300 --> 00:34:42.800
- I thought I told you to get out.
- Joe!

416
00:34:42.900 --> 00:34:45.900
- But we need these goods. sir.
- What you need is a lesson.

417
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:48.900
- When I say. "out." I mean out.
- No. wait. brother!

418
00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:50.700
Joe!
O-h. Joe!

419
00:34:51.700 --> 00:34:54.100
You'll pay for this on Judgment Day!

420
00:34:54.200 --> 00:34:55.440
All right. but 'til that day...

421
00:34:55.500 --> 00:34:58.000
don't show your faces around here.
Is that clear?

422
00:34:58.600 --> 00:35:02.200
Go on. Get back to your cow flops.
Go on. scat!

423
00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:06.300
Come on. Joe.
Wake up.

424
00:35:09.800 --> 00:35:12.600
Put him in a trough.
That'll wake him up.

425
00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:23.500
- Easy does it.
- Got a new sheriff.

426
00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:25.600
Better mind your own business.

427
00:35:25.700 --> 00:35:28.600
- How's that?
- Ask the Major.

428
00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:32.600
Major Harrison denies us the right
to make purchases in his store.

429
00:35:32.700 --> 00:35:34.100
Oh?

430
00:35:34.200 --> 00:35:36.600
- Now. that ain't right. is it?
- Oh. no.

431
00:35:36.700 --> 00:35:39.500
That's what I say.
Be right back. Easy...

432
00:35:39.600 --> 00:35:41.500
- Who is he?
- I don't know.

433
00:35:41.600 --> 00:35:43.400
He's wearing a star.

434
00:35:44.100 --> 00:35:46.200
Hold it. there.

435
00:35:47.500 --> 00:35:49.600
Give him what he asked for.

436
00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:52.100
You're kiddin'. I hope.

437
00:35:52.400 --> 00:35:53.600
No.

438
00:36:04.200 --> 00:36:06.700
Load it up on the wagon. and fast.

439
00:36:28.500 --> 00:36:31.400
The Major ain't gonna like this.

440
00:36:43.700 --> 00:36:46.300
What were you sayin' about the Major?

441
00:37:08.800 --> 00:37:10.100
Hey. you.

442
00:37:19.200 --> 00:37:20.400
Get him!

443
00:37:36.300 --> 00:37:37.300
Hey.

444
00:37:56.100 --> 00:37:57.700
About time someone took care of it.

445
00:37:57.800 --> 00:37:59.300
Hey. what's your name. Deputy?

446
00:37:59.400 --> 00:38:02.800
Hey. you gonna stay on as sheriff?

447
00:38:02.900 --> 00:38:05.600
He don't talk much. that's for sure.

448
00:38:06.900 --> 00:38:08.600
Hey. Deputy!

449
00:38:08.700 --> 00:38:11.000
Hey.
ain't you gonna stop and talk a minute?

450
00:38:43.400 --> 00:38:45.400
Here. there's one jack too many.

451
00:38:45.500 --> 00:38:48.500
No. here. there's one Major too many.

452
00:38:50.500 --> 00:38:53.300
Look. Major.
it'd be nice  if you told your men...

453
00:38:53.400 --> 00:38:55.300
not to bother the farmers anymore.

454
00:38:57.500 --> 00:39:00.500
It ain't nice to hurt
peaceful people like that.

455
00:39:00.900 --> 00:39:02.100
Now. if your men keep it up...

456
00:39:02.200 --> 00:39:03.800
I'm gonna have to get'em where it hurts.

457
00:39:03.900 --> 00:39:06.800
- You sure about that?
- Positive.

458
00:39:07.500 --> 00:39:10.300
Ahh. ahh. ahh. oh!

459
00:39:11.900 --> 00:39:14.100
One store destroyed...

460
00:39:14.200 --> 00:39:16.800
three heads split like overripe melons...

461
00:39:16.900 --> 00:39:20.300
one man wounded.
and one castrated. all in two hours.

462
00:39:20.400 --> 00:39:23.600
Just two hours I left you alone...
two hours.

463
00:39:24.100 --> 00:39:26.100
Well. you asked me to give you a hand.

464
00:39:26.400 --> 00:39:28.000
Not like that. beetle brain!

465
00:39:28.400 --> 00:39:31.200
If you'd only seen those girls' eyes...

466
00:39:33.300 --> 00:39:35.400
They looked like two frightened fawns.

467
00:39:35.800 --> 00:39:37.900
Two frightened fawns...

468
00:39:38.000 --> 00:39:41.300
they were probably two sluts
lookin' for customers.

469
00:39:45.200 --> 00:39:47.000
- Hey. where are you goin'?
- To the fawns.

470
00:39:47.100 --> 00:39:48.900
- No. you're comin' with me.
- Where?

471
00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:51.800
Home to get your rags and leave.

472
00:39:52.300 --> 00:39:54.300
- Well. thank you. Sheriff.
- You're welcome.

473
00:39:54.400 --> 00:39:56.800
This was a quiet town before you came...

474
00:39:56.900 --> 00:39:58.900
disgusting town. but quiet.

475
00:39:59.000 --> 00:40:00.900
Are you tellin' me?

476
00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:03.500
Sheriff. what are we gonna do
about his prisoners?

477
00:40:03.600 --> 00:40:05.900
Do we hang'em. or do we throw'em out?

478
00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:08.000
I quit.
I'm not gonna work for them no more.

479
00:40:08.100 --> 00:40:09.200
Ahh. throw'em out...

480
00:40:09.300 --> 00:40:12.400
all of'em.
including that Mexican jumping bean.

481
00:40:12.500 --> 00:40:14.400
Oh. come on. Bambino.
no sense holding a grudge.

482
00:40:14.500 --> 00:40:17.200
- Don't call me Bambino.
- Want me to call ya Sheriff?

483
00:40:17.300 --> 00:40:20.500
Don't call me at all.
not even if you're drownin'.

484
00:40:20.600 --> 00:40:21.400
Hey. with what authority...

485
00:40:21.500 --> 00:40:22.780
are you throwin' me out of town?

486
00:40:22.800 --> 00:40:24.600
Authority of the law.

487
00:40:24.700 --> 00:40:27.900
I wouldn't talk about
the law if I were you.

488
00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:30.600
What's that supposed to mean?

489
00:40:31.800 --> 00:40:34.600
Well. uh. remember.
you're not a real sheriff...

490
00:40:34.700 --> 00:40:37.600
just a common horse thief.
and not a very good one at that.

491
00:40:37.700 --> 00:40:40.600
- Evening. Sheriff.
- Hey. keep quiet.

492
00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:45.100
So?

493
00:40:45.200 --> 00:40:49.100
I'm stayin'. and with this pinned on.

494
00:40:50.700 --> 00:40:53.200
And a dollar a day plus meals.

495
00:40:56.300 --> 00:40:58.900
- That sounds like blackmail.
- Yeah. it does.

496
00:41:00.900 --> 00:41:03.400
All right. you stool pigeon.

497
00:41:03.500 --> 00:41:07.400
But if you start one more mess.
you'd better disappear.

498
00:41:10.100 --> 00:41:12.200
The deputy sleeps in the office.

499
00:41:14.900 --> 00:41:17.600
- Hi. there. Sheriff.
- Shut up.

500
00:41:17.700 --> 00:41:20.200
Hey. Sheriff... oh. it's you.

501
00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:28.300
- Out for trouble again. I see.
- Oh. I'm a peaceful man.

502
00:41:29.600 --> 00:41:31.000
Where ya goin'?

503
00:41:31.100 --> 00:41:34.800
The saloon.
just a little nip before goin' to bed.

504
00:41:34.900 --> 00:41:37.800
- Like to believe that.
- How about it?

505
00:41:37.900 --> 00:41:41.100
- Have one on me.
- Only one?

506
00:41:41.200 --> 00:41:44.300
- Well. forget it. then.
- Forget it. he”.

507
00:41:47.600 --> 00:41:52.200
Well. looks like the deputy sheriff
is layin' low tonight. huh?

508
00:41:53.100 --> 00:41:56.000
First chance I get.
I'll fix him for good.

509
00:41:56.100 --> 00:41:56.900
Yeah.

510
00:41:57.000 --> 00:41:59.000
- That dirty son of an old...
- Don't try it.

511
00:41:59.100 --> 00:42:00.800
He's quicker than a rattlesnake.

512
00:42:00.900 --> 00:42:04.500
Don't like the comparison.
but your friend's got a point.

513
00:42:04.600 --> 00:42:07.300
Don't try it.

514
00:42:17.100 --> 00:42:19.500
Let's get outta here.

515
00:42:58.900 --> 00:43:01.300
Never a night somethin' doesn't happen.

516
00:43:22.100 --> 00:43:23.800
I don't think I like that.

517
00:43:23.900 --> 00:43:26.400
What did you say about my old lady?

518
00:43:26.500 --> 00:43:29.000
You reach and start fight.

519
00:43:30.300 --> 00:43:32.700
I asked you a question.
What did you say...

520
00:43:32.800 --> 00:43:35.600
about my old lady?
- You heard it.

521
00:43:36.900 --> 00:43:40.100
Well. say it again.
Don't be afraid.

522
00:43:40.600 --> 00:43:43.100
Afraid of you?

523
00:43:46.200 --> 00:43:47.500
Huh?

524
00:43:50.900 --> 00:43:53.400
Afraid you got more cheek than brain.

525
00:44:01.800 --> 00:44:04.900
Hey. Sheriff... wake up!

526
00:44:05.600 --> 00:44:07.800
Sheriff!
Sheriff. wake up!

527
00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:09.800
Open in the name of the law!

528
00:44:10.300 --> 00:44:12.300
It's me. Jonathan!

529
00:44:12.600 --> 00:44:13.600
Oh!

530
00:44:13.700 --> 00:44:16.900
You better get your hide over to the saloon
right away!

531
00:44:17.000 --> 00:44:20.900
- What's happening now?
- Your brother is over there.

532
00:44:21.200 --> 00:44:23.600
Huh?
They killed him?

533
00:44:23.700 --> 00:44:26.600
Well. he was still standing when I left.

534
00:44:26.700 --> 00:44:29.500
But they'll make a sieve out of him
if you don't hurry!

535
00:44:29.600 --> 00:44:31.700
Yeah.

536
00:44:32.700 --> 00:44:34.100
Seven of us. Deputy...

537
00:44:34.200 --> 00:44:37.500
and you're only holdin'
six bullets in your gun.

538
00:44:37.800 --> 00:44:41.000
Now. I don't know if I make myself clear.

539
00:44:41.600 --> 00:44:43.700
Better pay your bar bill now.

540
00:44:43.800 --> 00:44:46.400
Don't wanna leave any debts behind.

541
00:44:46.500 --> 00:44:48.700
Now. I don't know if I made myself clear.

542
00:44:48.800 --> 00:44:51.200
- Hurry. Sheriff.
- Yeah. yeah.

543
00:44:53.400 --> 00:44:56.100
What's goin' on here?

544
00:44:56.200 --> 00:44:57.900
They offended the law.

545
00:44:59.100 --> 00:45:00.500
Law?

546
00:45:01.000 --> 00:45:02.500
Yes.

547
00:45:02.600 --> 00:45:05.400
They said I was a son of an old...

548
00:45:06.900 --> 00:45:09.100
That is serious.

549
00:45:09.400 --> 00:45:11.700
How are we gonna settle that. boys?

550
00:45:11.800 --> 00:45:15.100
If you didn't care to hide
behind that piece of tin...

551
00:45:15.200 --> 00:45:17.900
we could settle this among men.

552
00:45:20.700 --> 00:45:22.700
Aren't you gonna take it off?

553
00:45:22.800 --> 00:45:24.800
They are only nine.

554
00:45:29.000 --> 00:45:30.700
- Jonathan!
- Ahh!

555
00:45:30.800 --> 00:45:32.700
Take the guns.

556
00:45:40.400 --> 00:45:42.100
Here you go.

557
00:45:44.000 --> 00:45:45.500
Here.

558
00:45:51.200 --> 00:45:53.300
Close the door.

559
00:45:56.500 --> 00:45:58.000
Lock it!

560
00:46:10.200 --> 00:46:12.400
You gonna handle it alone?

561
00:46:16.400 --> 00:46:19.000
I just woke up.
You take your share.

562
00:46:21.900 --> 00:46:24.500
Wasn't a very bright idea.
my friend.

563
00:46:27.900 --> 00:46:29.300
Get him.
Get him.

564
00:46:30.600 --> 00:46:32.000
Stop it.

565
00:46:33.100 --> 00:46:34.600
- Push him.
- Oh!

566
00:46:35.500 --> 00:46:37.000
Hey. let me... let me go.

567
00:46:37.600 --> 00:46:39.200
Oh!

568
00:46:57.100 --> 00:46:58.200
No.

569
00:47:01.100 --> 00:47:02.000
Can I go to bed...

570
00:47:02.100 --> 00:47:04.200
or you got somethin' else
planned for tonight?

571
00:47:04.300 --> 00:47:06.600
Well. I really came for a drink.

572
00:47:09.700 --> 00:47:12.600
I'm sorry.
but I couldn't let them call ma an old...

573
00:47:12.700 --> 00:47:14.100
But it's true.

574
00:47:14.600 --> 00:47:16.900
Yeah. but she ain't that old.

575
00:47:20.500 --> 00:47:22.600
Ain't you got no ambition in life?

576
00:47:22.700 --> 00:47:24.400
Do somethin'.
Rustle cattle. hold up...

577
00:47:24.500 --> 00:47:28.300
a stagecoach. or play cards.
or somethin'.

578
00:47:28.400 --> 00:47:31.700
Once. you were a good card shark.
but do somethin'.

579
00:47:31.800 --> 00:47:35.400
Who's got the time?
I'm already busy doin' nothin'.

580
00:48:07.500 --> 00:48:08.800
Who are they?

581
00:48:08.900 --> 00:48:11.200
They're the farmers the Major wants out.

582
00:48:12.100 --> 00:48:15.800
- How come they're not armed?
- Oh. it's part of their religion.

583
00:48:16.200 --> 00:48:18.900
- They don't believe in violence.
- Huh?

584
00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:20.700
Oh. it's somethin' like that.

585
00:48:20.800 --> 00:48:23.100
Well. how do they manage
with the Major after 'em?

586
00:48:23.200 --> 00:48:25.900
Oh. with some prayers and broken bones.

587
00:48:30.200 --> 00:48:32.000
Welcome. brothers!

588
00:48:35.100 --> 00:48:36.700
Hey. who told him we were brothers?

589
00:48:36.800 --> 00:48:38.500
Hmm?
Not me.

590
00:48:38.800 --> 00:48:40.400
It is the Lord that sends you!

591
00:48:40.800 --> 00:48:43.700
Truth is. we was just passin' by!

592
00:48:43.900 --> 00:48:46.800
Then. come!
Come join us. brothers!

593
00:49:07.700 --> 00:49:10.500
Get off your horses and rest a while.

594
00:49:15.300 --> 00:49:17.500
It was good of you to come.

595
00:49:17.600 --> 00:49:20.800
We are truly indebted to you
for having aided our sisters...

596
00:49:20.900 --> 00:49:22.400
Sarah and Judith.

597
00:49:22.900 --> 00:49:26.100
They were innocent doves
surrounded by evil...

598
00:49:26.200 --> 00:49:29.000
but the Lord heard their prayers
and sent you to answer them.

599
00:49:29.100 --> 00:49:32.000
Yeah. it was approximately like that.

600
00:49:32.700 --> 00:49:35.100
Sure is peaceful around here.

601
00:49:35.200 --> 00:49:37.200
Just like paradise.

602
00:49:37.700 --> 00:49:40.000
And it is.
For that reason...

603
00:49:40.100 --> 00:49:42.600
we wouldn't want the
Major to contaminate it.

604
00:49:42.700 --> 00:49:44.200
You're right.

605
00:49:44.800 --> 00:49:45.800
You would honor us...

606
00:49:45.900 --> 00:49:47.800
if you would share our meager meal with us.

607
00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:49.800
Wanna share?

608
00:49:56.000 --> 00:49:57.400
Come.

609
00:50:11.100 --> 00:50:13.200
- Wash your hands first.
- Right.

610
00:50:27.400 --> 00:50:29.600
- Your guns. brothers.
- What?

611
00:50:30.100 --> 00:50:32.400
It is best not to sit
at the Lord's table...

612
00:50:32.500 --> 00:50:34.700
with symbols of violence.

613
00:50:36.700 --> 00:50:39.900
- Thank you. brother.
- Don't take 'em far away.

614
00:50:42.400 --> 00:50:43.700
Let us pray.

615
00:50:51.500 --> 00:50:52.800
Dear Lord...

616
00:50:53.000 --> 00:50:55.500
we are grateful to
you for these thy gifts...

617
00:50:55.600 --> 00:50:59.500
which we are about to receive
through your infinite goodness.

618
00:51:00.700 --> 00:51:03.200
And. Lord.
we ask you to bless and protect...

619
00:51:03.300 --> 00:51:06.100
our brethren who are
not with us at this time.

620
00:51:06.200 --> 00:51:08.800
- Amen.
- Amen.

621
00:51:09.100 --> 00:51:10.600
Amen.

622
00:51:30.700 --> 00:51:32.200
Mm-hmm.

623
00:51:33.700 --> 00:51:35.300
Hey. pass the bread down this way.

624
00:51:35.400 --> 00:51:36.800
Well. look at that.

625
00:51:46.400 --> 00:51:47.600
Oh.

626
00:51:49.800 --> 00:51:51.600
Yahoo!

627
00:51:55.400 --> 00:51:57.700
All the children and sisters leave.
quickly.

628
00:52:05.600 --> 00:52:08.200
I beg you to forgive their rudeness.

629
00:52:08.300 --> 00:52:11.300
They're like misguided children
who know not what they do.

630
00:52:21.000 --> 00:52:22.500
Hey!

631
00:52:37.400 --> 00:52:40.100
Brother Tobias!
My gringo.

632
00:52:42.600 --> 00:52:45.000
We were passing by when I say to my men...

633
00:52:45.200 --> 00:52:48.000
"why don't we go to pay a visit
to my friend. Tobias?"

634
00:52:48.100 --> 00:52:49.700
- Right?
- Right.

635
00:52:50.300 --> 00:52:51.200
If you care to join us.

636
00:52:51.300 --> 00:52:53.400
No. don't insist. brother.

637
00:52:53.500 --> 00:52:57.400
I don't like to take advantage
of your hospitality every day.

638
00:52:57.500 --> 00:52:58.400
Thank you. brother Mezcal...

639
00:52:58.500 --> 00:53:00.260
but you're always welcome
to share our table.

640
00:53:00.300 --> 00:53:03.500
Ahh. Si. well. then we'll take advantage.

641
00:53:07.800 --> 00:53:09.200
Hombre!

642
00:53:10.400 --> 00:53:12.500
Why don't you remind me
to take off my holster?

643
00:53:13.300 --> 00:53:15.000
Don't you know brother Tobias...

644
00:53:15.100 --> 00:53:17.400
doesn't like to see guns at his table?

645
00:53:18.800 --> 00:53:20.520
- Well. now you know.
- Your guns. brothers.

646
00:53:20.600 --> 00:53:22.900
- How about the knife?
- Here.

647
00:53:24.700 --> 00:53:27.200
- Thank you. brother.
- Here's another.

648
00:53:28.400 --> 00:53:30.800
- Bring the wine!
- Si. Señor.

649
00:53:31.400 --> 00:53:33.000
Quiet. everybody.
Now...

650
00:53:33.100 --> 00:53:35.600
I make a toast to brother Tobias.

651
00:53:36.200 --> 00:53:38.400
I said wine. not water.

652
00:53:38.600 --> 00:53:40.600
- Where's the wine?
- I'm sorry. brother.

653
00:53:40.700 --> 00:53:43.200
- It's against...
- Where's the wine?!

654
00:53:43.800 --> 00:53:45.400
Where's the wine?

655
00:53:47.100 --> 00:53:49.500
Get them in line!
Vamonos. cabron!

656
00:53:49.600 --> 00:53:51.700
- You. too!
- Everybody get in line.

657
00:53:51.800 --> 00:53:54.300
- You're too slow!
- Arriba!

658
00:53:56.300 --> 00:53:57.900
Not you. stupid.

659
00:54:08.600 --> 00:54:10.700
You no drink wine. eh?

660
00:54:13.900 --> 00:54:17.900
All right. you don't drink wine.
but you make love. no?

661
00:54:18.000 --> 00:54:20.200
No?
Cabron!

662
00:54:23.000 --> 00:54:24.500
Wait. brother. wait. please.

663
00:54:24.600 --> 00:54:27.100
You are not my brother no more!

664
00:54:28.800 --> 00:54:30.500
I think this one make love.

665
00:54:30.600 --> 00:54:32.800
Bueno. the other side now.

666
00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:38.200
How dare you hit one of my brothers?

667
00:54:39.500 --> 00:54:43.200
- Ask forgiveness.
- Forgiveness. please.

668
00:54:43.300 --> 00:54:46.200
- Hey. where are you going?
- Turn the other cheek.

669
00:55:02.600 --> 00:55:05.600
This one is new to me.
He's very pretty.

670
00:55:06.300 --> 00:55:09.300
Like this.
You. give me room.

671
00:55:45.600 --> 00:55:47.500
Hit him.

672
00:55:49.400 --> 00:55:51.300
- Me?
- Hmm.

673
00:56:06.400 --> 00:56:07.900
We go away now. huh?

674
00:56:12.700 --> 00:56:15.300
Brother. I tried to warn you...

675
00:56:15.400 --> 00:56:18.200
that my two guests here
belong to another belief.

676
00:56:18.300 --> 00:56:19.700
They rigidly observe the law...

677
00:56:19.800 --> 00:56:22.400
of an eye for an eye
and a tooth for a tooth.

678
00:56:22.500 --> 00:56:25.600
I'd say that you forgive them
and return some other time.

679
00:56:25.700 --> 00:56:27.600
Si. Si.

680
00:56:30.800 --> 00:56:33.200
- I kill him. gringo.
- Bueno. bueno. patron.

681
00:56:35.500 --> 00:56:39.400
I swear...
Mezcal don't forget this!

682
00:56:40.200 --> 00:56:42.100
Yeah. I can believe it.

683
00:56:45.000 --> 00:56:46.900
- Hee-yah!
- Hah!

684
00:56:57.500 --> 00:56:59.500
Brother Tobias. that was so brave.

685
00:56:59.600 --> 00:57:01.400
Are they really gone?

686
00:57:07.600 --> 00:57:09.700
Now. you can help yourselves.
You have their guns.

687
00:57:09.800 --> 00:57:10.700
If Mezcal comes back...

688
00:57:10.800 --> 00:57:12.520
one bullet in the fire
will change his mind.

689
00:57:12.600 --> 00:57:14.700
The Lord giveth life and the Lord taketh.

690
00:57:14.800 --> 00:57:17.200
Our weapons are faith and love.

691
00:57:17.600 --> 00:57:19.600
Well spoken. brother Tobias.

692
00:57:20.300 --> 00:57:22.600
Only love shall combat evil.

693
00:57:22.900 --> 00:57:24.400
It is the sacred word.

694
00:57:24.500 --> 00:57:28.000
"From my body. you shall have
the heat to warm your blood."

695
00:57:28.100 --> 00:57:31.500
"And from my breast. drink
the nectar to quench thy thirst."

696
00:57:31.600 --> 00:57:32.800
"And from my lips..."

697
00:57:32.900 --> 00:57:36.200
"you shall hear only words
of love for the Lord."

698
00:57:37.100 --> 00:57:38.700
Thus spake Ezekiel.

699
00:57:38.800 --> 00:57:40.600
He was damn right.

700
00:57:41.900 --> 00:57:44.300
- Your guns. brothers.
- Oh. and your hat. brother.

701
00:57:44.400 --> 00:57:45.200
Thank you.

702
00:57:45.400 --> 00:57:47.400
- Uh. if you need me...
- Us.

703
00:57:47.900 --> 00:57:50.800
If you need us.
you know where we are.

704
00:58:04.300 --> 00:58:05.600
Get movin'.

705
00:58:13.700 --> 00:58:15.300
Yah!

706
00:58:31.400 --> 00:58:32.800
God is with us.

707
00:58:44.300 --> 00:58:47.000
- Evening. Jonathan.
- Go to hell.

708
00:58:47.500 --> 00:58:50.000
He'll leave tomorrow.
Just passing through.

709
00:58:50.100 --> 00:58:51.500
In a pig's ear he is.

710
00:58:51.600 --> 00:58:53.600
He'll stay for the rest of his life.

711
00:58:53.700 --> 00:58:57.400
And from what's going on.
that won't be too long.

712
00:58:57.500 --> 00:59:01.800
Disgusting... disgusting people.

713
00:59:02.400 --> 00:59:06.200
Only safe thing left to do
is blow your brains out.

714
00:59:07.500 --> 00:59:09.500
All right. come and get it.

715
00:59:09.600 --> 00:59:12.400
That Mexican is so drunk
he can't stand up.

716
00:59:12.500 --> 00:59:15.000
Oh. he's fine.
He seemed a little sick before...

717
00:59:15.100 --> 00:59:16.688
so I gave him a couple of drops of whiskey.

718
00:59:16.700 --> 00:59:19.100
Well. wasn't that mighty nice of you?

719
00:59:19.200 --> 00:59:22.300
I think so. but I always say
everything wrong around here.

720
00:59:22.400 --> 00:59:24.500
Oh. shut up.

721
00:59:25.900 --> 00:59:27.900
Yeah. look at them.
Go on. eat my pork.

722
00:59:28.000 --> 00:59:29.800
Go on. eat up.
Huh.

723
00:59:30.200 --> 00:59:32.600
Who knows?
It may be your last meal.

724
00:59:33.300 --> 00:59:34.300
Why?

725
00:59:37.700 --> 00:59:40.000
'Cause I saw two new faces in town.

726
00:59:40.100 --> 00:59:42.900
Ooh. real ugly.

727
00:59:43.000 --> 00:59:44.800
And they don't promise any good.

728
00:59:44.900 --> 00:59:46.900
Oh.

729
00:59:51.200 --> 00:59:54.400
- Where are you goin'?
- To welcome them strangers.

730
00:59:54.600 --> 00:59:56.700
I thought you said
you weren't lookin' for trouble.

731
00:59:57.600 --> 00:59:59.300
I don't like people with ugly faces.

732
00:59:59.400 --> 01:00:02.400
Get the itch outta
your finger and stay put.

733
01:00:20.400 --> 01:00:22.000
Hmm.

734
01:00:22.900 --> 01:00:26.600
What would humanity have come to
without the horse?

735
01:00:28.000 --> 01:00:31.200
The great Caesar. Alexander the Great...

736
01:00:31.800 --> 01:00:34.000
the greats of Spain...

737
01:00:35.800 --> 01:00:38.900
would they really have been great
without the horse?

738
01:00:43.800 --> 01:00:45.900
Would this nation ever have been born...

739
01:00:46.000 --> 01:00:49.200
without the generous help
of that noble animal?

740
01:00:49.300 --> 01:00:51.600
Now. what is the best way
to pay our debt...

741
01:00:51.700 --> 01:00:54.800
if not to offer them a quiet.
green pasture...

742
01:00:54.900 --> 01:00:58.000
where they can eat
and procreate in peace?

743
01:00:59.700 --> 01:01:02.500
Therefore. I want that valley...

744
01:01:02.600 --> 01:01:04.700
at any cost.

745
01:01:05.600 --> 01:01:09.900
And if you convince the farmers to leave...

746
01:01:10.500 --> 01:01:14.600
I'll make it so worth your while
you'll be able to retire.

747
01:01:15.400 --> 01:01:17.500
That valley is already yours. Major.

748
01:01:17.600 --> 01:01:19.200
Good.

749
01:01:20.000 --> 01:01:21.300
First. however...

750
01:01:21.400 --> 01:01:25.100
I'd like you to take care of the sheriff
and his deputy.

751
01:01:25.400 --> 01:01:28.800
Their. uh. zeal is positively disturbing.

752
01:01:29.000 --> 01:01:32.500
You can start electing
a new sheriff as of now.

753
01:01:32.600 --> 01:01:34.600
That I will.

754
01:01:36.100 --> 01:01:38.000
You care for some sherry?

755
01:01:40.100 --> 01:01:42.300
It's wine. the best.

756
01:01:42.500 --> 01:01:45.900
Uh. no. thank you. Major.
not while working.

757
01:01:47.600 --> 01:01:51.000
That's what I call
professional seriousness.

758
01:01:54.600 --> 01:01:57.100
I advise you to watch the deputy.

759
01:01:57.200 --> 01:01:58.800
He's very fast.

760
01:01:59.700 --> 01:02:01.500
You hear that. Mortimer?

761
01:02:01.600 --> 01:02:04.900
The Major says the deputy is very fast.

762
01:02:10.200 --> 01:02:12.900
- Oh. yeah!
- All right. come on. let's go.

763
01:02:13.000 --> 01:02:14.600
You come this way.

764
01:02:54.100 --> 01:02:57.000
- Where are you goin'?
- Out- take a look around.

765
01:02:57.100 --> 01:02:58.900
It's a quiet day today.

766
01:02:59.000 --> 01:03:01.600
See that it ends up the way it started.

767
01:03:48.600 --> 01:03:50.100
Wait 'till Jack gets a hold of him.

768
01:03:50.200 --> 01:03:51.500
Yeah.

769
01:04:18.500 --> 01:04:21.700
That's the fast deputy. Mortimer.

770
01:04:32.400 --> 01:04:34.000
Hmm.

771
01:04:42.600 --> 01:04:45.400
Can I help you with somethin'. Deputy?

772
01:04:57.200 --> 01:05:00.500
Anything in particular
you're interested in?

773
01:05:00.600 --> 01:05:03.600
Uh. yeah.
Would you mind showing me your underwear?

774
01:05:14.100 --> 01:05:16.500
- Hey. what about the horses?
- There's no time!

775
01:05:18.000 --> 01:05:19.700
He said ten seconds!

776
01:05:53.800 --> 01:05:56.800
I suppose you got nothin' to do with this.
right?

777
01:05:59.800 --> 01:06:02.800
Sheriff. this was a peaceful town...

778
01:06:02.900 --> 01:06:04.900
before this madman came here.

779
01:06:05.000 --> 01:06:07.700
Now. he can't go around hittin'
and shootin' our good citizens...

780
01:06:07.800 --> 01:06:10.400
just because you gave him that star.

781
01:06:10.500 --> 01:06:13.800
In the name of this community.
I demand your resignation...

782
01:06:13.900 --> 01:06:15.700
and your deputy's. or I shall be forced...

783
01:06:15.800 --> 01:06:19.400
to speak to my personal friend.
the governor.

784
01:06:19.500 --> 01:06:22.100
Uh-huh. all right.

785
01:06:24.300 --> 01:06:26.800
We can't let him get away with it. Major.

786
01:06:26.900 --> 01:06:28.100
Hmm.

787
01:06:31.800 --> 01:06:34.300
Damn the day you ever came into the world.

788
01:06:34.400 --> 01:06:37.900
You're worse than the black plague
and a leprechaun.

789
01:06:42.100 --> 01:06:43.500
For the umpteenth time...

790
01:06:43.600 --> 01:06:45.600
what do you want me to do
with that Mexican?

791
01:06:45.700 --> 01:06:49.200
- Oh. throw him out.
- But he can't stand up.

792
01:06:49.700 --> 01:06:53.300
Give him some whiskey.
It'll make him go to sleep.

793
01:07:01.000 --> 01:07:03.000
Somethin' the matter?

794
01:07:03.200 --> 01:07:06.800
Nothin' important...
there's a reward out for me.

795
01:07:07.500 --> 01:07:11.000
The new sheriff I took this star from.
he ain't dead.

796
01:07:11.100 --> 01:07:15.100
He's lame.
He's lookin' for me all over the state.

797
01:07:15.600 --> 01:07:19.500
Now. he wants me to give him a hand
to find me.

798
01:07:27.500 --> 01:07:29.200
Hey. 200 dollars.

799
01:07:31.100 --> 01:07:33.200
You thinkin' of sellin' your own brother?

800
01:07:36.000 --> 01:07:37.100
That's an insult.

801
01:07:37.200 --> 01:07:39.500
I'd never do such a thing
for only 200 bucks.

802
01:07:42.200 --> 01:07:43.600
Wanna come with me?

803
01:07:45.800 --> 01:07:46.900
Where?

804
01:07:48.000 --> 01:07:49.400
Hmm.

805
01:07:51.100 --> 01:07:52.688
You're takin' advantage
because you know I'd never...

806
01:07:52.700 --> 01:07:55.200
shoot you. right?
- Sure.

807
01:07:57.200 --> 01:07:59.300
Why in the hell don't you wise up?

808
01:07:59.400 --> 01:08:01.600
Go back to New Orleans to Mama.

809
01:08:01.700 --> 01:08:05.300
Bring her a couple of girls
and go into business with her.

810
01:08:06.900 --> 01:08:09.100
Now. beat it.
Move!

811
01:08:09.800 --> 01:08:13.300
Well. so long.
Hope to see ya again someday.

812
01:08:14.000 --> 01:08:15.500
I don't.

813
01:08:44.200 --> 01:08:47.000
If I really wanted to stay. I would!

814
01:08:50.100 --> 01:08:51.600
I don't think so!

815
01:09:39.000 --> 01:09:41.000
Helen. come and help me!

816
01:09:45.800 --> 01:09:48.200
- Billy. you get it.
- I'll have it ready in a few seconds.

817
01:09:49.900 --> 01:09:51.100
Hand me that ax.

818
01:09:51.200 --> 01:09:53.100
Myrtle. get this kid back to the wagon.
will ya?

819
01:09:53.200 --> 01:09:54.800
He's always in the way.

820
01:09:56.300 --> 01:09:58.800
It's good to see you again. brother.

821
01:09:58.900 --> 01:10:00.800
What breeze brings you here?

822
01:10:00.900 --> 01:10:03.800
Well. actually. weren't no breeze.

823
01:10:03.900 --> 01:10:04.900
I'm goin' home.

824
01:10:05.000 --> 01:10:06.500
Just passin' through to say goodbye.

825
01:10:07.400 --> 01:10:09.400
You've been our guardian angel.

826
01:10:09.500 --> 01:10:11.600
May the Lord be with you.
But if you should choose...

827
01:10:11.700 --> 01:10:14.500
to remain with us. my son.
you're more than welcome.

828
01:10:14.600 --> 01:10:17.400
Thank you. but I really have to go.

829
01:10:18.500 --> 01:10:20.400
- It's a pity.
- Hmm.

830
01:10:20.500 --> 01:10:22.500
Well. as you wish.

831
01:10:23.000 --> 01:10:25.400
But before you leave. I know...

832
01:10:25.600 --> 01:10:28.100
that Sarah and Judith would like to
thank you personally.

833
01:10:28.800 --> 01:10:30.300
They're down by the creek.

834
01:10:30.500 --> 01:10:32.100
Oh. down by the creek?

835
01:10:32.300 --> 01:10:34.300
I'll get someone to fetch them.

836
01:10:34.400 --> 01:10:37.200
Ah. don't bother. chief.
I'll be going by that way.

837
01:10:37.300 --> 01:10:39.100
They'll be happy to see you.

838
01:10:56.900 --> 01:10:59.500
- Oh. look. it's Trinity!
- Hi!

839
01:10:59.600 --> 01:11:02.000
- Welcome. brother!
- Howdy!

840
01:11:02.400 --> 01:11:05.700
- Come on in!
- Hey. the water is fine!

841
01:11:05.800 --> 01:11:07.000
Come on!

842
01:11:15.100 --> 01:11:17.100
Hey. it's marvelous.
Come on in.

843
01:11:17.600 --> 01:11:20.100
The water is warm.
Don't be afraid.

844
01:11:23.000 --> 01:11:25.200
Come on.
Don't be a sissy.

845
01:11:26.300 --> 01:11:28.800
Oh. he's comin' in. horse and all.

846
01:11:29.900 --> 01:11:33.100
Hey.
the invitation didn't include your horse.

847
01:11:33.200 --> 01:11:34.700
Well. he can swim.
I can't.

848
01:11:36.000 --> 01:11:38.100
But the water is only up to here.

849
01:11:38.200 --> 01:11:40.100
Oh. well. in that case...

850
01:11:42.700 --> 01:11:44.800
What is he doing?

851
01:11:53.000 --> 01:11:55.700
You know. when we saw you
for the first time...

852
01:11:55.800 --> 01:11:57.600
we thought that it
would've been wonderful...

853
01:11:57.700 --> 01:11:59.100
if you joined our community.

854
01:11:59.200 --> 01:12:02.500
Yeah. it kinda passed my mind. too.

855
01:12:05.800 --> 01:12:08.400
You could've lived with us.
Made a home with devoted...

856
01:12:08.500 --> 01:12:11.100
wives to take care of you and serve you.

857
01:12:11.500 --> 01:12:14.100
- Wives?
- Uh-huh. wives.

858
01:12:14.200 --> 01:12:15.888
Didn't you know our
faith accepts the state...

859
01:12:15.900 --> 01:12:18.300
or fact of polygamy?

860
01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:20.800
Huh?

861
01:12:45.400 --> 01:12:47.200
Hey. it's gettin' deeper.

862
01:12:57.400 --> 01:13:00.100
Before we start shingling.
we better raise the chimney.

863
01:13:00.200 --> 01:13:01.700
You're right. brother.

864
01:13:01.900 --> 01:13:03.800
Help me. brother.

865
01:13:12.300 --> 01:13:14.200
Yeah. right.

866
01:13:15.600 --> 01:13:17.300
- Bye.
- Bye.

867
01:13:27.500 --> 01:13:29.200
You'll be leavin' right away?

868
01:13:29.300 --> 01:13:32.600
Well. if the invitation still stands...

869
01:13:32.700 --> 01:13:34.800
we thought we'd stay on for a day or so.

870
01:13:34.900 --> 01:13:36.000
By all means.

871
01:13:36.100 --> 01:13:38.700
Whatever is ours is yours to share.

872
01:13:44.700 --> 01:13:47.600
Ahh. chh-chh-chh.
Ahh. chh-chh-chh.

873
01:13:48.100 --> 01:13:51.000
There's no way to stop the Major?

874
01:13:51.700 --> 01:13:53.700
He ain't the type to give in.

875
01:13:53.800 --> 01:13:56.700
He'll come chargin' down here
before you know it.

876
01:13:56.800 --> 01:13:59.400
Our fate is in the hands of the Lord.

877
01:13:59.500 --> 01:14:00.888
Yeah. but he doesn't carry a gun either.

878
01:14:00.900 --> 01:14:04.700
Can't get much help there.
Look. I don't think...

879
01:14:04.800 --> 01:14:07.100
the Lord would take it wrong
if you defend yourselves.

880
01:14:07.200 --> 01:14:09.100
We cannot kill our fellow man.

881
01:14:09.700 --> 01:14:11.400
But they ain't your fellow man.

882
01:14:11.500 --> 01:14:13.800
They're lower than rattlesnakes.

883
01:14:13.900 --> 01:14:17.100
You can't go on turnin'
the other cheek forever.

884
01:14:17.200 --> 01:14:19.300
We shall see what God wills.

885
01:14:19.400 --> 01:14:22.000
I hope he wills a couple of guns.

886
01:14:22.100 --> 01:14:24.600
You could get rid of the whole bunch.

887
01:14:24.700 --> 01:14:26.900
A few at a time. of course.

888
01:14:27.500 --> 01:14:30.600
Listen. I suggest that...

889
01:14:34.700 --> 01:14:36.600
Hey. look.

890
01:14:40.300 --> 01:14:42.600
Hey. Ma. there's two strangers here!

891
01:14:54.800 --> 01:14:57.200
Who might they be. brother?

892
01:14:57.700 --> 01:15:00.800
Judging from appearances.
I'd say they were...

893
01:15:00.900 --> 01:15:02.800
wayfarers tired from a long journey.

894
01:15:02.900 --> 01:15:06.500
Or two outlaws
escaping across the desert.

895
01:15:06.600 --> 01:15:08.900
Also. the Lord crossed the desert.

896
01:15:09.000 --> 01:15:13.500
Yeah. but he didn't have
the U.S. Rangers on his tail.

897
01:15:13.600 --> 01:15:16.200
Go see what they want.
If they start making trouble...

898
01:15:16.300 --> 01:15:18.000
I'll be right behind you.

899
01:15:44.100 --> 01:15:45.300
May I?

900
01:15:45.400 --> 01:15:48.900
"Give drink to the thirsty."
says the Holy Word.

901
01:16:02.300 --> 01:16:04.000
If I'm not mistaken...

902
01:16:04.100 --> 01:16:06.500
it also says to give food to the hungry.
right?

903
01:16:06.600 --> 01:16:08.300
Wrong.

904
01:16:14.600 --> 01:16:16.500
You're Weasel. ain't ya?

905
01:16:17.900 --> 01:16:19.600
Yeah.

906
01:16:24.100 --> 01:16:25.700
And you're Timmy.

907
01:16:27.400 --> 01:16:30.600
And you're lookin' for the Bambino.

908
01:16:31.300 --> 01:16:33.500
You wouldn't know where he's been. huh?

909
01:16:33.700 --> 01:16:36.200
Yeah. waitin' for you to get here.

910
01:16:41.400 --> 01:16:44.100
What in the hell are you up to now?

911
01:16:45.000 --> 01:16:46.400
Hey. boss!

912
01:16:46.800 --> 01:16:49.600
I've been rottin' here
for weeks waitin' for ya.

913
01:16:49.700 --> 01:16:53.100
I was beginning to think
they strung you both up.

914
01:16:53.400 --> 01:16:56.100
We were sidetracked out on the trail.

915
01:16:56.800 --> 01:16:59.300
We saw somebody following us out...

916
01:16:59.800 --> 01:17:03.300
so we detoured around the canyon
and shot him off his horse.

917
01:17:03.500 --> 01:17:06.300
It was a sheriff.
a lame-legged sheriff.

918
01:17:06.400 --> 01:17:07.588
He weren't really lookin' for us.

919
01:17:07.600 --> 01:17:10.100
We just happened to be
goin' the same way.

920
01:17:10.200 --> 01:17:11.900
- Did you fix him for good?
- Well. uh...

921
01:17:12.000 --> 01:17:14.300
Well. almost...
Timmy got him in the good leg.

922
01:17:14.400 --> 01:17:17.000
Then we broke his crutches.

923
01:17:17.100 --> 01:17:18.600
Yeah.

924
01:17:20.000 --> 01:17:22.300
What are you doin' with that star?

925
01:17:22.600 --> 01:17:24.400
- Hidin' behind the law.
- Huh?

926
01:17:24.500 --> 01:17:28.200
Now. listen to me.
There's a beautiful job for us...

927
01:17:28.300 --> 01:17:31.000
a ripe plum just waitin' to be picked.

928
01:17:31.100 --> 01:17:32.400
Cattle?

929
01:17:34.100 --> 01:17:36.300
- Steeds.
- Did you hear that?

930
01:17:36.600 --> 01:17:38.800
- Yeah.
- The most gorgeous herd...

931
01:17:38.900 --> 01:17:41.700
of unbranded stallions you ever seen.

932
01:17:42.800 --> 01:17:45.800
- How'd you know I was here?
- I told them.

933
01:17:46.100 --> 01:17:48.300
- Oh. no.
- Now. listen a minute. Bambino.

934
01:17:48.400 --> 01:17:50.700
I don't want...

935
01:17:52.600 --> 01:17:53.800
I don't wanna listen.

936
01:17:59.700 --> 01:18:00.888
Look. I just wanted to tell you...

937
01:18:00.900 --> 01:18:03.900
- Oh. go on. get.
- Hey. hold on.

938
01:18:04.000 --> 01:18:06.200
Didn't you hear what the boss said?

939
01:18:06.300 --> 01:18:08.400
Hmm?

940
01:18:14.400 --> 01:18:15.300
Hey. wait up.
There's somethin' important...

941
01:18:15.400 --> 01:18:18.200
I gotta tell ya.
Comin' to town...

942
01:18:18.300 --> 01:18:20.140
I saw the Major headin'
for the Mexican border.

943
01:18:20.200 --> 01:18:22.400
You know what that means?

944
01:18:23.400 --> 01:18:26.800
It means that he's
gonna join up with Mezcal.

945
01:18:26.900 --> 01:18:28.900
Them farmers won't have a chance.

946
01:18:35.800 --> 01:18:37.700
Look.
if you help me get rid of the Major...

947
01:18:37.800 --> 01:18:41.000
I'll. uh. get married.

948
01:18:41.100 --> 01:18:43.100
- You'll what?
- I'll get married.

949
01:18:43.200 --> 01:18:45.500
- To who?
- To Sarah or Judith...

950
01:18:45.600 --> 01:18:48.200
I haven't decided yet.
But I'm gonna settle down...

951
01:18:48.300 --> 01:18:50.500
with the farmers...

952
01:18:51.600 --> 01:18:53.500
Forever.

953
01:19:17.300 --> 01:19:20.600
- Forever?
- Yes. forever.

954
01:19:22.300 --> 01:19:25.500
- I want to forget the past.
- Hmm?

955
01:19:35.700 --> 01:19:38.600
Swear on our old lady.

956
01:19:40.300 --> 01:19:43.800
May she become an honest woman
if I'm tellin' a lie.

957
01:19:50.800 --> 01:19:53.000
All right. it's a deal.

958
01:19:53.500 --> 01:19:55.700
I'll help you...

959
01:19:56.900 --> 01:19:59.600
but then we go separate ways...

960
01:19:59.900 --> 01:20:02.800
or I'll make sure you
really forget the past.

961
01:20:02.900 --> 01:20:06.000
- Thanks. You won't be sorry.
- Yeah.

962
01:20:08.500 --> 01:20:11.200
Uh. listen. about taking care of the Major.

963
01:20:11.300 --> 01:20:13.020
- I was thinkin'.
- You don't have to think!

964
01:20:13.100 --> 01:20:16.700
- I'll do the thinkin'!
- Exactly what I was thinking.

965
01:20:20.600 --> 01:20:22.500
Idiot!

966
01:20:40.200 --> 01:20:42.700
Oh. that is the very nice Major.

967
01:20:43.000 --> 01:20:45.400
He's got a lot of dinero. muchachos.

968
01:20:52.300 --> 01:20:53.800
Bienvenido.

969
01:20:58.100 --> 01:21:00.200
You sit here. in the shade. no?

970
01:21:00.300 --> 01:21:01.700
Thank you.

971
01:21:03.400 --> 01:21:04.600
Fuera. fuera!

972
01:21:04.700 --> 01:21:07.500
- Buenos Dias. Major.
- You. too!

973
01:21:08.400 --> 01:21:11.200
So. how is my worst enemy. huh?

974
01:21:11.600 --> 01:21:13.700
Your best friend now.

975
01:21:14.100 --> 01:21:17.000
But your men shoot us just yesterday.

976
01:21:19.100 --> 01:21:22.300
You see. Mr. Mezcal.
if you steal my horses...

977
01:21:22.400 --> 01:21:26.400
I'll have to have you shot.
But if you work for me...

978
01:21:26.600 --> 01:21:29.500
I'll give them to you.
20 of them...

979
01:21:29.600 --> 01:21:31.400
for chasing the Mormons out of the valley.

980
01:21:32.500 --> 01:21:36.300
Major. for 20 stallions.
Mezcal conquer Texas.

981
01:21:36.400 --> 01:21:37.600
But how about the...

982
01:21:37.700 --> 01:21:40.500
Uh. I mean.
is there some way in particular...

983
01:21:40.600 --> 01:21:43.200
you would like us
to kill those insects. huh?

984
01:21:43.300 --> 01:21:46.200
- That's your business.
- Yeah.

985
01:21:46.300 --> 01:21:49.300
There's only one thing
I don't like. Major.

986
01:21:49.400 --> 01:21:50.600
And that is?

987
01:21:50.900 --> 01:21:53.600
It's that I prefer to steal the horses.

988
01:21:53.700 --> 01:21:57.600
Si. I do the job for you.
and you let me steal 20 horses.

989
01:21:58.000 --> 01:22:00.300
To work for pay is humiliating.

990
01:22:00.500 --> 01:22:02.700
Better to steal.
There's more emotion.

991
01:22:05.700 --> 01:22:07.500
All right. all right.

992
01:22:07.700 --> 01:22:11.900
Jeff. tell the men to let Mr. Mezcal
steal 20 horses...

993
01:22:14.000 --> 01:22:16.400
Without shooting this time.

994
01:22:16.500 --> 01:22:19.300
Muy bien.
Hombre. wine. now.

995
01:22:19.400 --> 01:22:23.200
Let's drink to the 20 stallions.

996
01:22:28.700 --> 01:22:32.000
- When do we attack?
- When they expect it least.

997
01:22:32.100 --> 01:22:33.580
In a few days.
send one of your men...

998
01:22:33.600 --> 01:22:36.400
to look around and then report back to me.

999
01:22:36.500 --> 01:22:38.900
I send Emiliano.
He would be able...

1000
01:22:39.000 --> 01:22:42.900
to crawl under your sombrero
without you knowing it.

1001
01:22:46.800 --> 01:22:49.800
I figure there'll be about 20 of 'em.
and every one...

1002
01:22:49.900 --> 01:22:52.700
a gunslinger.
So if you don't use...

1003
01:22:52.800 --> 01:22:56.300
your guns.
they'll make fertilizer out of you.

1004
01:22:56.400 --> 01:22:59.100
Our faith prohibits violence.

1005
01:22:59.200 --> 01:23:01.100
You don't believe the
four of us can hold off...

1006
01:23:01.200 --> 01:23:03.300
the Major's crowd. do you?

1007
01:23:06.700 --> 01:23:09.800
We'll have to ask the Lord
for a temporary dispensation.

1008
01:23:09.900 --> 01:23:11.300
Better get it in a hurry. brother.

1009
01:23:13.100 --> 01:23:16.600
Brothers. we must make this decision now.

1010
01:23:16.700 --> 01:23:18.900
- Yes.
- There's no way out otherwise.

1011
01:23:19.000 --> 01:23:22.400
All right. but only for self-defense.

1012
01:23:22.500 --> 01:23:25.000
We will not kill.

1013
01:23:29.200 --> 01:23:31.800
Well. at least that's somethin'.

1014
01:23:33.900 --> 01:23:35.800
Okay. let's get going.

1015
01:23:38.500 --> 01:23:41.600
All right. line up now.
That's it.

1016
01:23:47.300 --> 01:23:48.988
If someone comes swinging with his right...

1017
01:23:49.000 --> 01:23:51.300
what do you do?
You block with your left...

1018
01:23:51.400 --> 01:23:54.000
and counter with your right.
You.

1019
01:23:56.900 --> 01:24:00.500
I repeat... block with your left...

1020
01:24:00.600 --> 01:24:02.800
and counter with your right.
Got it?

1021
01:24:02.900 --> 01:24:05.700
- Yes. brother.
- All right. let's try it.

1022
01:24:10.700 --> 01:24:13.200
I said block with your left.
not your right.

1023
01:24:15.500 --> 01:24:18.100
See what happens?
It's a question of timing.

1024
01:24:20.500 --> 01:24:23.400
If someone comes swinging a pole at you.
what do you do?

1025
01:24:23.500 --> 01:24:26.000
- I don't know.
- Well. you duck.

1026
01:24:26.100 --> 01:24:27.700
- Yeah.
- Grab him.

1027
01:24:27.800 --> 01:24:30.000
- Yeah.
- And pull him down!

1028
01:24:30.100 --> 01:24:32.000
- That clear?
- Yes. brother.

1029
01:24:32.100 --> 01:24:35.500
- Okay. ready?
- Ready.

1030
01:24:35.600 --> 01:24:38.200
- Ugh!
- Oh. no.

1031
01:24:38.300 --> 01:24:41.000
Now. watch how it's done.
Watch.

1032
01:24:41.100 --> 01:24:43.900
Now. look at me.

1033
01:24:44.000 --> 01:24:47.900
- Watch this.
- You ready?

1034
01:24:48.000 --> 01:24:49.700
Ahh!

1035
01:24:53.600 --> 01:24:57.400
Remember. the most important thing is
to be fast.

1036
01:24:58.100 --> 01:24:59.900
Is that clear?

1037
01:25:01.400 --> 01:25:03.300
- Ahh!
- Ahh!

1038
01:25:04.000 --> 01:25:05.800
Now. then. when you...

1039
01:25:07.200 --> 01:25:09.400
Experience is always the best teacher.

1040
01:25:09.500 --> 01:25:11.800
Now.
if you ain't much at swinging your arms...

1041
01:25:11.900 --> 01:25:14.500
you can always use your feet. like me.

1042
01:25:14.600 --> 01:25:16.900
Ow! Oh'.
Ow!

1043
01:25:17.600 --> 01:25:19.400
- Ready?
- Mm-hmm.

1044
01:25:22.200 --> 01:25:24.900
All right. get up. and you try now.

1045
01:25:31.200 --> 01:25:32.200
Ahh!

1046
01:25:32.800 --> 01:25:34.100
Oh. Pete.

1047
01:25:34.200 --> 01:25:36.800
Easy. brother. Get up.
Up you go.

1048
01:25:38.900 --> 01:25:41.000
You get him in a lock and bounce him...

1049
01:25:41.100 --> 01:25:42.300
up and down like this.

1050
01:25:43.700 --> 01:25:45.600
Brother.
perhaps you're going ahead too fast.

1051
01:25:45.700 --> 01:25:47.400
I have no time to waste.

1052
01:25:50.600 --> 01:25:53.500
Don't worry.
He'll be all right.

1053
01:25:54.900 --> 01:25:58.000
- You know. I was just thinking.
- If it's advice. save your breath.

1054
01:25:58.100 --> 01:26:01.000
It ain't advice.
I only want your opinion.

1055
01:26:04.000 --> 01:26:05.800
All right. go on.

1056
01:26:06.600 --> 01:26:08.700
Do you suppose there's
somebody spying on us...

1057
01:26:08.800 --> 01:26:10.700
under that sombrero?

1058
01:26:14.800 --> 01:26:16.200
- Then you duck.
- Hmm.

1059
01:26:16.300 --> 01:26:19.900
- It's a serious possibility.
- That's what I thought.

1060
01:26:20.100 --> 01:26:21.800
- Weasel!
- When you swing around...

1061
01:26:22.000 --> 01:26:24.600
- Come here a minute.
- Try it by yourselves.

1062
01:26:24.700 --> 01:26:26.600
All right. now. by the numbers.

1063
01:26:26.700 --> 01:26:28.100
Let's try it.

1064
01:26:30.700 --> 01:26:33.400
I think there's a spy sittin'
under that sombrero...

1065
01:26:33.500 --> 01:26:36.300
up there on the hill.
Bring him down...

1066
01:26:37.100 --> 01:26:38.600
Alive.

1067
01:26:48.200 --> 01:26:50.500
Somethin' wrong. Sheriff?

1068
01:26:51.000 --> 01:26:52.300
Nothin' important.

1069
01:26:52.400 --> 01:26:55.200
There's only someone up there on the hill.

1070
01:26:55.300 --> 01:26:57.900
Weasel has gone to invite him down.

1071
01:26:58.000 --> 01:27:01.900
- Heaven protect our friend.
- Better protect the spy.

1072
01:27:17.100 --> 01:27:20.000
If you're smart. you'll talk.

1073
01:27:20.100 --> 01:27:21.700
Who sent ya?

1074
01:27:22.100 --> 01:27:25.000
Emiliano doesn't betray. gringo.

1075
01:27:33.700 --> 01:27:37.700
Emiliano tells everything.
I'm one of Mezcal's men.

1076
01:27:38.000 --> 01:27:41.600
The Major. he said
he promised Mezcal 20 stallions...

1077
01:27:41.700 --> 01:27:44.800
if we chase the farmers out of here.

1078
01:28:06.600 --> 01:28:10.900
Listen. you ain't goin' ahead
with that plan without me.

1079
01:28:11.000 --> 01:28:14.200
I know you too well.
You're like an open book.

1080
01:28:17.200 --> 01:28:20.700
Oh. yeah?
Then let's see if you read right.

1081
01:28:23.100 --> 01:28:27.000
You wanna take the Mexicans' place.
get the 20 horses. and then...

1082
01:28:33.500 --> 01:28:35.200
Am I wrong?

1083
01:28:39.400 --> 01:28:40.900
You read right.

1084
01:28:41.000 --> 01:28:43.800
I'm glad you're beginning
to use your head.

1085
01:28:45.900 --> 01:28:47.600
Listen. Emiliano...

1086
01:28:47.700 --> 01:28:51.700
would you do us a favor
in exchange for your stinkin' skin?

1087
01:28:51.800 --> 01:28:54.800
- Claro Que Si. hombre.
- That's the spirit.

1088
01:29:00.400 --> 01:29:03.200
- Hold it. right there!
- No. no. don't shoot!

1089
01:29:03.300 --> 01:29:04.700
It's me. Emiliano!

1090
01:29:04.800 --> 01:29:06.900
Mezcal sent us to steal the horses.

1091
01:29:07.000 --> 01:29:09.200
All right. but make it quick.

1092
01:29:16.100 --> 01:29:17.800
Buenas noches. Señor.

1093
01:29:17.900 --> 01:29:20.300
Just take your 20 horses
and clear outta here.

1094
01:29:20.400 --> 01:29:21.600
Si. Si.

1095
01:29:27.700 --> 01:29:29.600
I'll take the two white ones.

1096
01:29:30.200 --> 01:29:32.800
Two. three. four. five.

1097
01:29:33.100 --> 01:29:35.100
- How did it go with the farmers?
- Oh. fine.

1098
01:29:35.200 --> 01:29:36.600
Six.
Muy bien.

1099
01:29:36.700 --> 01:29:39.400
- Seven. eight. nine. ten.
- Any killings?

1100
01:29:39.500 --> 01:29:41.600
Eleven.
Todos muertos.

1101
01:29:41.700 --> 01:29:43.300
- All dead?
- Twelve. thirteen.

1102
01:29:43.400 --> 01:29:46.500
Right... children. women.
old ladies. all dead.

1103
01:29:46.700 --> 01:29:49.100
- Fourteen. fifteen. sixteen.
- Holy Hannah. Killed 'em all?

1104
01:29:49.200 --> 01:29:50.300
Seventeen.
Ah. Si.

1105
01:29:51.000 --> 01:29:52.200
Cats. dogs. everybody.

1106
01:29:52.600 --> 01:29:54.600
- Eighteen. nineteen.
- What a massacre!

1107
01:29:54.700 --> 01:29:56.700
Si. it was a nice massacre.

1108
01:29:56.800 --> 01:29:59.800
- Twenty. twenty-one. twenty-two...
- Hey.

1109
01:29:59.900 --> 01:30:02.400
...twenty-three. twenty-four.
- Hey. you were supposed...

1110
01:30:02.500 --> 01:30:04.200
to take 20.
- Twenty-five. twenty-six.

1111
01:30:04.300 --> 01:30:05.900
Be quiet or I lose count. no?

1112
01:30:06.200 --> 01:30:08.900
Thirty. thirty-one.
thirty-two. thirty-three...

1113
01:30:09.000 --> 01:30:11.000
thirty-four. thirty-five.

1114
01:30:13.500 --> 01:30:15.800
- Where is the sheriff?
- Who are you?

1115
01:30:15.900 --> 01:30:17.500
Who are you?

1116
01:30:18.300 --> 01:30:19.800
I'm Jonathan Swift.

1117
01:30:20.100 --> 01:30:21.800
I keep the office in order...

1118
01:30:21.900 --> 01:30:23.400
and the sheriff's gone out of town.

1119
01:30:23.500 --> 01:30:25.800
He is. huh?
When's he comin' back?

1120
01:30:25.900 --> 01:30:29.300
Well. that depends.
If he catches 'em...

1121
01:30:29.400 --> 01:30:32.100
he should be back around. uh...
- Catches who?

1122
01:30:32.900 --> 01:30:36.000
- Horse thieves.
- Are these here the men?

1123
01:30:36.900 --> 01:30:38.600
Oh. the sheriff.

1124
01:30:38.700 --> 01:30:40.500
Yeah. there's a certain similarity.

1125
01:30:40.600 --> 01:30:42.600
- There is?
- That's them.

1126
01:30:42.700 --> 01:30:45.200
That's them.
That really is them.

1127
01:30:45.300 --> 01:30:47.800
Well. do you know
where they were headed?

1128
01:30:47.900 --> 01:30:51.100
Listen. well. they told me
they were going to the... border!

1129
01:30:51.200 --> 01:30:52.700
Yeah. remember the border...

1130
01:30:52.800 --> 01:30:54.800
Nail those there outside the office.

1131
01:30:54.900 --> 01:30:56.888
- Yes. siree. right away. Sheriff.
- If I ever catch up with them...

1132
01:30:56.900 --> 01:30:58.700
they'll pay for this.
- Yes. siree...

1133
01:30:58.800 --> 01:31:01.600
went to the border.
We'll take care of...

1134
01:31:01.700 --> 01:31:04.300
the whole thing. Sheriff.
Don't you worry about...

1135
01:31:04.400 --> 01:31:06.400
Whiskey. whiskey.

1136
01:31:07.800 --> 01:31:10.000
Up you go.
You. too.

1137
01:31:13.300 --> 01:31:15.800
All the children are loaded into the wagon.
Sheriff.

1138
01:31:16.100 --> 01:31:18.900
- All right. over here!
- Weasel. watch the kids.

1139
01:31:20.500 --> 01:31:21.600
Hear. men...

1140
01:31:22.900 --> 01:31:26.300
take your boys and get around
back of the house.

1141
01:31:27.400 --> 01:31:30.000
So. you wouldn't know where Tobias is.

1142
01:31:30.100 --> 01:31:32.500
I think he went down to the river
with some of his men.

1143
01:31:32.600 --> 01:31:33.800
- And the horses?
- Huh?

1144
01:31:33.900 --> 01:31:36.200
The horses. damn you!
Where'd you put 'em?

1145
01:31:36.300 --> 01:31:38.200
Oh. the horses.

1146
01:31:38.400 --> 01:31:41.000
They're under cover. safe and sound.

1147
01:31:41.100 --> 01:31:44.400
Hey. brother lookout!
You seeing anything?

1148
01:31:45.300 --> 01:31:48.400
No. brother Sheriff. nothing!

1149
01:31:52.800 --> 01:31:56.200
I mean. yes!
They're coming!

1150
01:31:56.500 --> 01:31:57.800
They're coming!

1151
01:31:58.700 --> 01:32:00.000
Get ready.

1152
01:32:02.100 --> 01:32:03.300
Hah!

1153
01:32:25.700 --> 01:32:27.900
It's old Jonathan!

1154
01:32:34.100 --> 01:32:35.300
Whoa.

1155
01:32:36.800 --> 01:32:38.200
Whoa.

1156
01:32:41.600 --> 01:32:43.600
Major is looking for you. Sheriff.

1157
01:32:43.700 --> 01:32:45.600
What's he want?

1158
01:32:46.200 --> 01:32:48.000
Justice. I guess.

1159
01:32:48.100 --> 01:32:49.800
A herd of his horses was stolen...

1160
01:32:49.900 --> 01:32:51.600
and he wants the help of the law...

1161
01:32:51.700 --> 01:32:53.900
to punish the rustlers
and get his horses back.

1162
01:32:54.300 --> 01:32:57.100
- Well. I can't help him now.
- I didn't think so.

1163
01:32:57.500 --> 01:32:59.800
You're not keeping all those
horses for yourself. are ya?

1164
01:32:59.900 --> 01:33:02.800
- What horses?
- What horses?

1165
01:33:03.000 --> 01:33:04.600
The Major's horses.

1166
01:33:04.900 --> 01:33:07.000
Did you come here to tell me that?

1167
01:33:07.100 --> 01:33:09.900
- Yeah. among other things.
- Such as?

1168
01:33:10.800 --> 01:33:13.400
Well. a man came to town today...

1169
01:33:14.300 --> 01:33:17.100
Mustache. star on his chest. crutches...

1170
01:33:18.300 --> 01:33:20.700
a typical crippled sheriff...

1171
01:33:21.200 --> 01:33:23.500
and he was lookin' for the fellas
who made him that way.

1172
01:33:24.100 --> 01:33:27.000
- I sent him to the border.
- Good.

1173
01:33:27.100 --> 01:33:28.900
- Is that all?
- Oh. no. no. no.

1174
01:33:29.000 --> 01:33:31.100
Uh. the Major will be here any minute.

1175
01:33:32.000 --> 01:33:33.200
Thanks. old man.

1176
01:33:34.000 --> 01:33:35.900
You're welcome.

1177
01:33:36.200 --> 01:33:37.700
I want my share.

1178
01:33:37.800 --> 01:33:39.800
Yeah. that figures.

1179
01:33:39.900 --> 01:33:41.600
What'd you bring him for?

1180
01:33:41.700 --> 01:33:43.500
Well. I couldn't leave him in town.

1181
01:33:43.600 --> 01:33:45.088
Uh. he's got a tendency to tell the truth.

1182
01:33:45.100 --> 01:33:47.500
He's an alcoholic. you know?

1183
01:33:56.400 --> 01:33:57.700
Ho!

1184
01:33:58.900 --> 01:34:00.100
Get these guns.

1185
01:34:00.200 --> 01:34:02.200
Put the Mexican in that wagon
and keep him drunk.

1186
01:34:02.300 --> 01:34:05.000
Yes. siree. partner.
Hah!

1187
01:34:13.200 --> 01:34:15.500
- Where the devil did Tobias go?
- Tobias?

1188
01:34:15.600 --> 01:34:18.100
- Yeah. Tobias.
- Right there. boss.

1189
01:34:24.900 --> 01:34:26.700
I thought you ran out on us.

1190
01:34:26.800 --> 01:34:29.400
No. we were working.
brother. working very hard.

1191
01:34:29.500 --> 01:34:30.800
That reminds me. boss.

1192
01:34:30.900 --> 01:34:33.400
Shouldn't we start diggin' a few graves...

1193
01:34:33.500 --> 01:34:35.700
now that we have the time?
- A few graves?

1194
01:34:36.200 --> 01:34:38.500
You don't wanna turn this place
into a cemetery. do you?

1195
01:34:38.600 --> 01:34:40.900
How do you think we're gonna
hold off the Major?

1196
01:34:41.100 --> 01:34:42.300
With faith.

1197
01:34:43.600 --> 01:34:44.800
Hmm.

1198
01:34:45.300 --> 01:34:47.900
Faith is an impenetrable fortress.

1199
01:34:48.900 --> 01:34:51.000
As cynical as the Major maybe...

1200
01:34:51.100 --> 01:34:54.800
he would not shoot at defenseless
women and children.

1201
01:34:55.200 --> 01:34:57.100
He could be right.

1202
01:35:17.200 --> 01:35:18.600
What do you think?

1203
01:35:18.700 --> 01:35:21.600
Would you shoot at a bunch
of women and kids?

1204
01:35:24.300 --> 01:35:26.800
Not the kids anyway.

1205
01:35:27.300 --> 01:35:29.100
Well. if you wouldn't do it...

1206
01:35:29.200 --> 01:35:31.800
then the Major certainly isn't gonna do it.

1207
01:35:31.900 --> 01:35:34.500
Now. what's on your mind?

1208
01:35:34.900 --> 01:35:37.000
You're the one that does the thinking...

1209
01:35:37.100 --> 01:35:40.600
and you came up with
a good idea this time. too.

1210
01:35:43.600 --> 01:35:44.700
Hmm.

1211
01:35:50.300 --> 01:35:53.300
All right.
but if the faith trick don't work...

1212
01:35:53.400 --> 01:35:55.100
this fella is gonna be bright red.

1213
01:36:08.800 --> 01:36:12.300
They're coming!
They're coming!

1214
01:36:33.000 --> 01:36:35.500
He's playing his last card.

1215
01:36:44.700 --> 01:36:46.400
Move in!

1216
01:36:47.100 --> 01:36:48.600
Slowly!

1217
01:37:02.700 --> 01:37:04.700
Hah!
Hah!

1218
01:37:05.200 --> 01:37:06.900
Yah!
Yah!

1219
01:37:21.000 --> 01:37:24.500
Well. aren't you going to welcome me.
old man?

1220
01:37:26.800 --> 01:37:29.100
Your silence won't keep
me from destroying...

1221
01:37:29.200 --> 01:37:31.400
your dignified poverty.

1222
01:37:31.500 --> 01:37:33.900
- Why waste time. Major?
- Quiet.

1223
01:37:37.800 --> 01:37:40.000
There is work to be done.

1224
01:37:41.400 --> 01:37:42.700
Gentlemen...

1225
01:37:43.000 --> 01:37:45.400
today will be a hard day for you...

1226
01:37:45.500 --> 01:37:48.300
but you'll go home happy
to have earned your money...

1227
01:37:48.400 --> 01:37:51.000
honestly for once.

1228
01:37:56.300 --> 01:37:59.900
Destroy everything they've built.
beginning with that house...

1229
01:38:00.000 --> 01:38:02.700
but please without yelling
and making too much of an uproar.

1230
01:38:02.800 --> 01:38:04.900
You know I detest noise.

1231
01:38:05.200 --> 01:38:07.100
Burn their wagons and the tents...

1232
01:38:07.200 --> 01:38:09.700
and scatter those miserable cows.

1233
01:38:09.800 --> 01:38:11.700
Then we'll depart and...

1234
01:38:13.100 --> 01:38:15.800
let Mr. Mezcal take care of the rest.

1235
01:38:17.600 --> 01:38:19.900
Lost your tongue. old man?

1236
01:38:20.000 --> 01:38:22.200
You've lost your battle. Major...

1237
01:38:22.300 --> 01:38:24.500
from the very moment
you descended that hill.

1238
01:38:27.500 --> 01:38:30.100
The opinions of others.
no matter how idiotic...

1239
01:38:30.200 --> 01:38:32.100
should be respected.

1240
01:38:32.200 --> 01:38:34.100
I certainly will not
be the one to violate...

1241
01:38:34.200 --> 01:38:36.100
the rules of good manners.

1242
01:38:36.200 --> 01:38:37.400
Jeff.

1243
01:38:47.800 --> 01:38:50.100
Jeff. tear the house down.

1244
01:38:56.200 --> 01:38:59.500
All right. boys. start hacking.

1245
01:39:19.900 --> 01:39:22.500
Je... Jeff!
Jeff!

1246
01:39:23.300 --> 01:39:25.000
- Yeah. Major?
- Come on back.

1247
01:39:25.600 --> 01:39:27.600
- Hold it. boys!
- Yeah.

1248
01:39:30.100 --> 01:39:31.800
There's been a variation in my plan.

1249
01:39:32.100 --> 01:39:34.300
Want us to start with the wagons and tents?

1250
01:39:35.400 --> 01:39:37.200
No. I don't think so.

1251
01:39:37.800 --> 01:39:39.200
Start driving out the cows?

1252
01:39:39.800 --> 01:39:41.500
Why should those animals bother you?

1253
01:39:42.000 --> 01:39:44.800
Well. I'm just not understanding.
What should I do?

1254
01:39:46.100 --> 01:39:48.300
Respect the principles of these people.

1255
01:39:51.400 --> 01:39:53.900
- Put down your guns.
- What?

1256
01:39:54.100 --> 01:39:56.300
